This is the current version of this document. You can provide feedback on this policy to the document author - refer to the Status and Details on the document's navigation bar.
Section 1 - Background and Purpose
(1)
The purpose of the
La Trobe University Commercial Activities Guidelines
is to provide a set of principles and outline the process for the development and conduct of commercial activities of the University, in order to maximise the benefits and to minimise the risks to the University of undertaking such activities.
(2)
The Guidelines are made pursuant to sections 53 to 56 and other provisions of the
La Trobe University Act 2009
(the Act) and are approved by the Minister.
Section 2 - Scope
(3)
There are eight (8) guidelines:
Guideline 1 – Prior to entering a commercial activity;
Guideline 2 – Indemnities;
Guideline 3 – After entering a commercial activity;
Guideline 4 – Register of commercial activities and report;
Guideline 5 – Section 48 of the Act – corporations and joint ventures;
Guideline 6 – University controlled entities;
Guideline 7 – Section 47 of the Act – Audit of income and expenditure of the University;
Guideline 8 – Making Assessments.
